    <string name="main_extra_1">Servers are tested from top to bottom. With a threshold, the first server within it is tried first. If the field is empty or 0, all servers are tested and the lowest ping is selected.</string>
    <string name="main_extra_2">In automatic mode the app checks the connection and selects another chosen server if the current server fails.</string>
    <string name="main_extra_3">Subscription age is checked when the app opens. Outdated subscriptions refresh when internet is available.</string>
    <string name="main_extra_4">After a failed reconnection, subscriptions of selected servers are refreshed before retrying.</string>
    <string name="main_extra_5">Subscriptions are downloaded and refreshed only over Wi-Fi.</string>
    <string name="main_extra_6">Show system notifications when the connection is lost or waiting for internet.</string>
    <string name="main_extra_7">One round tests and attempts to connect to available selected servers. Zero means unlimited rounds.</string>
    <string name="main_extra_8">Maximum subscription servers tested concurrently. Actual concurrency depends on device memory.</string>
    <string name="main_extra_9">Fraction of each subscription tested concurrently. For example, 5 means one fifth.</string>
    <string name="main_extra_10">If the subscription has fewer servers than this number, all are tested at once. Otherwise the selected fraction applies.</string>
    <string name="main_extra_11">Upper limit for concurrent tests when using a proportion. The device may test fewer servers at once.</string>
    <string name="main_extra_12">Milliseconds to wait for a server response. A timeout yields n/a.</string>
    <string name="main_extra_13">Minutes before a subscription becomes outdated and can refresh in the background. After an error, the next automatic attempt is at least one hour later.</string>
    <string name="main_extra_14">Proportion calculates the number of tests per subscription. Count sets a fixed limit. The device may reduce concurrency when memory is low.</string>
